= The Factory Councils

The workers' and soldiers' councils of November are losing ground to the new republic, but the factory councils are still alive in the big plants.

- @build: Build up the councils patiently.
- @occupy: Push the councils to occupy the factories.
- @easy_discard

@build
subtitle: Slow gains in worker support, scaled by the districts that follow us.
choose-if: lock_councils < 2
unavailable-subtitle: The [+ leading_faction_adj +] line forbids council work.
on-arrival: worker_support += 2 + 4*loyal_share; militancy += 3; unionist_satisfaction += 3

Communist shop stewards win seats on council after council.

@occupy
subtitle: Inspires the radicals, and brings the police.
choose-if: lock_councils < 2
unavailable-subtitle: The [+ leading_faction_adj +] line forbids council work.
on-arrival: militancy += 12; repression += 8; worker_support += 3; ultraleft_satisfaction += 10; offensive_satisfaction += 5; unionist_satisfaction -= 5; stability -= 3

Red flags fly over the factory gates, for now.
